Dana, per your request Prewitt performed an independent moisture assessment=
 of the tenant slabs on floors 12 through 19 last week. Memo attached.<br /=
>
<br />
We ran anhydrous calcium chloride testing per ASTM F1869 at nine locations.=
 Moisture vapor emission rates came back between 2.9 and 3.4 pounds per 1,0=
00 square feet per 24 hours, against the 5 pound limit published for the ca=
rpet tile adhesive that covers most of the area. On that basis our opinion =
is that the slabs are within tolerance for the scheduled resilient flooring=
 and that the specified epoxy vapor barrier is not required for this instal=
lation.<br />
<br />
We are aware the design team's consultant reported high in-situ RH numbers.=
 We would note that the two test methods measure different things and that =
the calcium chloride result is the one the flooring manufacturer's own lite=
rature references.
